Z||000000||BroCar 87||03-18-2000||01:02 AM||||Hey guys, I recently bought a 1987 pontiac fiero. The test drive was good but when i brought it home, i began to see a few problems. First off, when I crank my engine up, i have to wait a second for a squeal to occur. It sounds like a belt squeal but it only does it on the start up. <BR>Number two: I can't accelerate off the line fast or it backfires in the throttle body. i had the deck lid up and air filter cover off, and mashed the accelerater, and BANG, POOF a puff of smoke and a quite loud popping noise came. This doesn't happen if i slowly accelerate through the RPM's though. If i keep the RPM's up to around 1200 at a red light it has no trouble going. It just hates low RPM's. <BR>Sorry about the long message but if any one has any ideas or suggestions...please help!!  thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||03-18-2000||03:48 AM||||My belt squealed on startup for a few seconds, tightened the belt and it went away for awhile. When the squeal came back the waterpump was hard to turn by hand when cold.  Replaced the waterpump.  The next year the symptoms came back and it was the alternator.  Its always something.<P>Something like not enough fuel when the butterfly is opened rapidly.  I can't think of how to narrow that down right now (late night tequila) but if nobody else jumps in by tomorrow I promise to sober up and help.<P>BOGGWHAAAAAAAAAAAAA...I'm gone||||reg||12
Z||000002||BroCar 87||03-18-2000||01:23 PM||||YEA THATS WHAT I WAS THINKING ABOUT THE SQEAL, I JUST REPLACED THE ALTERNATOR. SO I BELIEVE IT IS THE WATERPUMP.<BR>ALSO, WHEN THE CAR SPUTTERS, THE CHECK ENGINE LIGHT COMES ON. THE BATTERY LIGHT ALSO COMES ON ONCE IN A WHILE. SO I AM STARTING TO BELIEVE THAT THERE IS AN ELECTRICAL PROBLEM I AM GOING TO GET IT CHECKED OUT SOON SO I WILL LET YOU KNOW. THANKS ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||03-18-2000||01:53 PM||||Last thing you want to do is yell when somebody has a hangover  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||03-18-2000||08:10 PM||||If the car is not "seeing" the additional throttle, it won't know when to add additional fuel. I'd test the throttle position sensor (TPS), and maybe the MAP sensor. The TPS voltage should vary from about "zero" to about 5 volts, depending on throttle opening. If you're getting a "check engine" light, there are probably some codes stored.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||03-19-2000||03:34 AM||||are your plug wires cracked?  replace them<P>check to see if your timing is off||||reg||1
